# Copy this file to detect.env (same directory) to override defaults.
# Optional - every value below has a sensible default if this file is
# absent. chmod 600 not required (nothing secret lives here).

# Where hailo-apps was cloned and installed (see SETUP.md step 3).
# HAILO_APPS_DIR=/home/pi/.local/share/hailo-apps

# Camera source, passed to face_recognition.py's --input flag.
#   usb           - a USB webcam at /dev/video0 (simplest, most reliable -
#                    recommended default, see SETUP.md's camera note)
#   rpi           - Raspberry Pi Camera Module via picamera2
#   libcamera     - Raspberry Pi Camera Module via the libcamerasrc
#                    GStreamer element directly (alternative to rpi;
#                    known to sometimes fail to find the camera when
#                    picamera2 itself works fine - see SETUP.md)
#   /dev/video2   - an explicit V4L2 device path
# CAMERA_SOURCE=usb

# Uncomment if running headless (no monitor attached) - required by
# Hailo's own app, which expects a display environment to exist even
# when nothing is actually rendering to a screen.
# HEADLESS_DISPLAY=:0
